@title Rolling back a bad game client patch
@subtitle Drift Harbor, Quillfeather Interactive
@author Live Ops
@date 2026-10-13

kpi Crash rate | above 2% | for 15 min | bad
kpi Login failures | above 5% | for 10 min | bad
kpi Last good build | 4.12.3

!!! Do not roll back if the patch contained a database schema migration. Rolling back after a schema migration corrupts player inventories.

## When to roll back

After a patch release, roll back when either condition holds:

- Crash rate is above 2% of sessions for 15 minutes.
- Login failures are above 5% for 10 minutes.

! The Live Ops lead must approve in the #liveops-war-room channel.

## Do not roll back if

The patch contained a database schema migration, such as migration 0087 in patch 4.13. Older clients cannot read the new schema, so go forward with a hotfix instead.

## Rollback steps

1. Stop the bleeding
-- Pause the deploy pipeline.
-- Set matchmaking to maintenance mode with the in-game message "Back soon".
2. Point players to the last good build
-- In the release console, set the live manifest to build 4.12.3.
-- Invalidate the CDN cache, which takes about 10 minutes.
3. Verify
-- Install the build on 3 test accounts, one each on PC, console and mobile.
-- Confirm login and a full match.
4. Reopen in stages
-- Let in 10% of players.
-- Go to 25% after 5 minutes.
-- Go to 50% after 5 more minutes.
-- Go to 100% after another 5 minutes if the crash rate stays under 1%.
5. Communicate
-- Post a status update within 30 minutes of the decision.
-- Schedule compensation of 500 gems for every active account.

